cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the entry below."
title: "Keeping the Referent in the DARK: Anchor-Preserving Token Compression for Privacy-Aware Inference on IoT Logs"
abstract: >-
  IoT device logs are long, identifier-dense, and routinely pasted into
  language-model prompts, where the entity a question names is also the value
  that must not be forwarded. Redaction removes the value and the handle the
  reader needs; compression keeps the handle and drops the record carrying the
  answer. DARK keeps that record and aliases the values inside it: a
  training-free, model-free routing rule over the pair (sensitive, relevant)
  that is budget-bounded and leak-free.
